Subject: [PATCH 18/40] docs(HOST, FORMAT): never restart an existing user via
 start; restart needs the latest committed snapshot; timers across document
 versions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

start resets seq, so the host's idempotency keys user:seq:index (HOST §1.4)
repeat and an idempotent CRM/outbox silently drops the second order's
create_order/save_address. Lost snapshot: restart with a placeholder
snapshot carrying the seq high-water mark. Also document stale-snapshot
restart and what happens to timers renamed/moved by a new document version.
Regression test: audit/engine_timers/check_host_contract.py (FAIL before, PASS after).

(cherry picked from commit 998a5395e518aa9ec09b625e0e20e22a1fe4538a)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
